---
import Divider from "../../../../components/ui/Divider.astro";
import Layout from "../../../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { Code } from "astro-expressive-code/components";

//#region CodeSnippets
const Bug1 = `function addTax(price) {
  let taxed = price * 1.08;
  return taxed;
}

console.log(addTax(50));
console.log(taxed);`;
const Bug2 = `let total = 100;

function addFee(total) {
  total = total + 5;
}

addFee(total);
console.log(total);`;
const Bug3 = `let rate = 0.08;

function priceWithTax(amount) {
  let rate = 0.2;
  return amount * (1 + rate);
}

console.log(priceWithTax(100));`;
const Bug4 = `function record() {
  let count = 0;
  count = count + 1;
  console.log(count);
}

record();
record();
record();`;
//#endregion
---

<Layout>
  <div class="container my-4">
    <div class="row justify-content-center">
      <div class="col-sm-12 col-md-10">
        <a href="/courses/ap-csp/" class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-light mb-3">
          <i class="si-arrow-left"></i> Back
        </a>

        <h1>Debug Challenge: Scope</h1>

        <Divider variant="8" classes="mb-5" />

        <section id="objective">
          <h2>Objective</h2>

          <p>Four short programs about where a variable lives. Two of them run perfectly and give the wrong answer, which is the harder kind.</p>

          <p>
            <b>Three kinds of mistake.</b> A <b class="text-sn-red">syntax
            error</b> stops the program before it runs. A{" "}
            <b class="text-sn-orange">reference error</b> runs until it hits the
            bad name, so you get partial output and then a crash. A{" "}
            <b class="text-sn-yellow">logic error</b> runs cleanly and gives the
            wrong answer.
          </p>

          <p><b>Three of these four are logic errors.</b></p>
        </section>

        <hr />

        <section id="bugs">
          <h2>The Four Programs</h2>

          <hr class="my-4" />

          <h3>Bug 1</h3>

          <p>This should print the tax. It crashes on the last line.</p>

          <Code code={Bug1} frame="code" lang="javascript" title="Bug 1" class="mb-3" />

          <p><b>Also:</b> Say in one sentence where <code>taxed</code> actually exists, and for how long.</p>

          <hr class="my-4" />

          <h3>Bug 2</h3>

          <p>This should add 5 to the running total. The total never changes.</p>

          <Code code={Bug2} frame="code" lang="javascript" title="Bug 2" class="mb-3" />

          <hr class="my-4" />

          <h3>Bug 3</h3>

          <p>This should use the shop's rate. It uses the wrong one.</p>

          <Code code={Bug3} frame="code" lang="javascript" title="Bug 3" class="mb-3" />

          <p><b>Also:</b> Both rates are defined and neither is a typo. What decides which one wins?</p>

          <hr class="my-4" />

          <h3>Bug 4</h3>

          <p>This should count three calls. It prints 1 three times.</p>

          <Code code={Bug4} frame="code" lang="javascript" title="Bug 4" class="mb-3" />
        </section>

        <hr />

        <section id="submit">
          <h2>Submit</h2>

          <p>For each program: which kind, one sentence on what was wrong, and the corrected line.</p>

          <p>Worth <b>3 points</b>, graded on completion.</p>
        </section>

        <h1 class="text-center mt-5 text-sn-theme border border-primary slow-flash">
          Commence Debugging
        </h1>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
